            "review_title": "Review at 108eatery",
            "review_text": "Bijou.Haus\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam428 contributions\n0\nWONDERFUL INTRODUCTION TO VEGAN\nFeb 2019 • Family\n108Eatery is a small joint located inside the compound of the Landscape Architecture Association at 28 Thao Dien, District 2, Ho Chi Minh City.\n\nOwn and managed by a Korean lady, 108Eatery serves a very small menu with only 6 main courses, including a garden salad.\n\nI have never been a fan of vegan food and selecting 108Eatery as the introduction point was certainly the right decision ... so much so that I have gone back for lunch a few times since the first visit!\n\nOf all the main courses on the menu, with the exception of the Garden Salad which I have never tried, I'd recommend the Temple Bibimbap with Sesame Soy Sauce (No Chili, No Garlic) as being the best. At VND130,000, this is an affordable, healthy and greatly delicious lunch!\n\nThe only issue I have is 108Eatery is its short opening hours, from 11:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m.!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten March 24, 2019",
